  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "Harmonized multimodal atlases now align human, macaque, marmoset, and mouse basal ganglia cell taxonomies across spatial and single-cell modalities.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cross-species harmonization of basal ganglia cell taxonomies across human, macaque, marmoset, and mouse. A multiomic atlas of 1.8M primate basal ganglia nuclei identifies 61 conserved cell types and maps disease risk to populations. A companion spatial transcriptomics atlas covers over one million cells per species, integrated with snRNA-seq. A BICAN multimodal atlas spanning four species integrates single-cell transcriptomics. HOMBA provides a harmonized ontology and 3D reference atlases onto which cellular taxonomies are mapped. What is new is the joint use of shared ontology, spatial reference frames, and provenance tracking. NIMP manages donors, brain slabs, sequencing and provenance across 11 labs, supplying the data-management layer for these atlases.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
